All New Dragons

2
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:21,000
Book of Dragons is a fantasy, animation, action film directed by Steve Hickner.

3
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:28,500
So you want to be a dragon trainer do you?

4
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:36,000
Prepare yourself for adventure, excitement and training as Hiccup, Astrid, Toothless and Gobber tell the legend
behind the Book of Dragons and reveal insider training secrets about new, never-before-seen dragons.

5
00:05:37,500 --> 00:05:43,500
Hiccup (voice), played by Jay Baruchel.

6
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:51,000
Gobber (voice), played by Craig Ferguson.

7
00:07:52,500 --> 00:07:58,500
Astrid (voice), played by America Ferrera.

8
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:06,000
Fishlegs (voice), played by Christopher Mintz-Plasse.

9
00:10:07,500 --> 00:10:13,500
Bork (voice), played by Jim Cummings.

10
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:21,000
Bork's Wife (voice), played by Tress MacNeille.

11
00:12:22,500 --> 00:12:28,500
Dragon (Chinese: 武俠; pinyin: Wǔ xiá) is a 2011 martial arts film directed by
Peter Chan, and starring Donnie Yen, Takeshi Kaneshiro and Tang Wei.

12
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:36,000
In this Hong Kong-Chinese co-production, Yen also
served as the film's action director.

13
00:14:37,500 --> 00:14:43,500
It premiered on 13 May 2011 at the 2011 Cannes Film
Festival in the Midnight Screenings category.

14
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:51,000
Donnie Yen and Peter Chan presided over the lighting of a 3591-square-metre billboard for Dragon that broke the record in the
Guinness Book of World Records for its size, a record previously held by a poster for a Michael Jackson album.

15
00:16:52,500 --> 00:16:58,500
The tone is lighthearted.
